# LeakSanitizer suppressions.
#
# GNU readline never frees a handful of internal allocations (keymaps,
# terminal state, the line buffer) before the process exits. These show up
# under AddressSanitizer as leaks originating in libreadline's xmalloc, even
# though our own cleanup (rl_clear_history, freeing rl_line_buffer) is correct.
# Suppress only those so genuine leaks in our code are still reported.
leak:libreadline
leak:xmalloc
